WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:08.920 align:start position:19%
In 1863, the excavator Giuseppe Fiorelli
has an idea. Pour liquid plaster into

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:13.600 align:start position:19%
the hollow, let it harden, chip away the
ash.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.240 align:start position:19%
What emerges stops the world cold. A dog
twisted in agony, still chained to its

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.120 align:start position:19%
post. A mother clutching her child. A
man covering his face as if the heat

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:29.480 align:start position:19%
were happening right now.
And here is the eeriest part. The bread

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:34.160 align:start position:19%
survived. Loaves of bread stamped with
the baker's seal sit carbonized in the

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:38.040 align:start position:19%
ovens exactly as they were left that
morning.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:42.520 align:start position:19%
Walnuts on a table, eggs in a bowl, a
purse of coins dropped in the street.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:45.920 align:start position:19%
Pompeii is not a ruin.
It is a paused morning.

